WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.803
If you're a fan of "The Witcher,"&nbsp;
you've already seen the news.

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:08.100
Can the Netflix fantasy series really&nbsp;
survive without Henry Cavill?

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.878
Liam Hemsworth will take over the role&nbsp;
of Geralt from Henry Cavill in Season 4,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.878 --> 00:00:15.600
for reasons that may or may not&nbsp;
have something to do with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.760
latter's recently revitalized&nbsp;
career as the DCEU's Superman.

00:00:20.109 --> 00:00:23.520
Hemsworth certainly has the looks&nbsp;
and chops to portray the stoic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:28.620
powerful Geralt of Rivia. However, Cavill&nbsp;
owns the role so thoroughly that many fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:34.080
have been reflexively hitting the eject button&nbsp;
after the recast news, which is a pretty clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:38.286
portent of doom for a franchise that's&nbsp;
named after its main character's day job.

00:00:38.286 --> 00:00:42.640
To use an analogy that befits Cavill,&nbsp;
every live-action version of Superman is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.680
going to be compared to Christopher&nbsp;
Reeve sooner or later.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:50.400
Likewise, Hemsworth now faces the seemingly&nbsp;
insurmountable task of carrying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:54.000
his beloved predecessor's silver&nbsp;
wig with adequate gruff and grace.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.440
Recasts like this have been pulled off&nbsp;
before — just ask the James Bond franchise.

00:00:58.929 --> 00:01:01.329
"People who want to stay alive play it safe."

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:03.918
"Please stay alive."

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:09.120
The difference here is that if Hemsworth&nbsp;
turns out to be a George Lazenby, it seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:13.380
unlikely that the viewers — or Netflix, for that&nbsp;
matter — will give "The Witcher" another chance.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:17.940
Probably the biggest thing that favors "The&nbsp;
Witcher's" Hemsworth era is the vast wealth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:22.980
of stories the show has hitherto left untapped.&nbsp;
There are still tons of plotlines that can really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:28.500
grab the fans' attention. Going by sheer cultural&nbsp;
significance alone, this means the show is almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:33.120
honor-bound to soften the blow of recasting&nbsp;
by diving headfirst into "The Wild Hunt."

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:38.580
The show has already revealed that the Wild&nbsp;
Hunt plays a role in things to come. Season 2&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:43.740
prominently features Voleth Meir, who turns out&nbsp;
to be a dark elf affiliated with the Wild Hunt.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:49.620
The Hunt itself also makes a brief, but suitably&nbsp;
ominous appearance in the season finale. As such,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:52.980
it should be just a matter of time&nbsp;
before this crew comes calling for Ciri.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:55.680
Here's a crucial question&nbsp;
about the show's survival,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:59.220
though. When will the Wild Hunt&nbsp;
start making moves? Introducing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:03.120
the otherworldly antagonists could easily&nbsp;
keep the show going for a good few seasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:08.340
and given the fact that Cavill is leaving after&nbsp;
the next season, the most effective time for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:13.020
Wild Hunt's proper introduction would be in&nbsp;
the Season 3 finale. This would provide an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:18.000
irresistible cliffhanger that could bring&nbsp;
fans back next season, Cavill or no Cavill.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.480
Henry Cavill originally committed&nbsp;
to "The Witcher" for seven seasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:26.400
and since the Nilfgaardian storyline will&nbsp;
likely swallow a whole bunch of Season 3 hours,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:31.560
the Wild Hunt could indeed chill out for the&nbsp;
majority of the season, only to make its charge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:36.540
at the optimal moment for Hemsworth to tag in&nbsp;
for Season 4. However, get the timing wrong,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:40.260
and there's the risk that a notable portion&nbsp;
of viewers will clock out with Cavill.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:44.040
Like it or not, it seems that Season 4&nbsp;
will definitely be a watershed moment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:48.480
for "The Witcher." If the show can manage its&nbsp;
sprawling cast of characters, introduce cool&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:53.580
enough plotlines, and handle the transition from&nbsp;
Cavill to Hemsworth with grace, it has conquered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:58.920
a challenge that puts Geralt's worst in-universe&nbsp;
enemies to shame, and is effectively as invincible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:04.799
as long as Netflix's algorithms smile on it. If&nbsp;
not ... well, at least it was fun while it lasted.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:08.700
"The Witcher" has all the tools to make&nbsp;
the change work. But when the pressure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:10.800
is mounting and the biggest&nbsp;
star of the show is leaving,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:15.660
many people might suddenly have suggestions&nbsp;
on how to tinker with the premise, or put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:21.120
overt focus on certain characters. Perhaps new,&nbsp;
non-canon characters that decidedly shouldn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:25.560
be introduced will be introduced anyway. Maybe&nbsp;
there will be a temptation to take unnecessary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:30.540
liberties with some storylines from the source&nbsp;
material, or needless shortcuts with others.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:34.800
If "The Witcher" can't resist tinkering with&nbsp;
what works — either to take attention away&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:38.400
from the recasting, or in an honest&nbsp;
attempt to provide fire support for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.571
the new lead — the show just&nbsp;
might be in serious trouble.

